  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nCurrent development in Greene/Fayette Counties looks to be firing on\na w-e boundary that was in nrn IL/IN about 4 hours ago. More storms\nare beginning as well in ncntl/ne IN. As of this moment, the CWA will\nbe adjusting to the neutrally unstable atmosphere in the wake of a\nstrong tstm cold pool. Around daybreak, outflow spread out fairly \nequally across the CWA. Funneling in air behind it early this \nafternoon may be playing with the timing/placement of storms, of \nwhich hasn't been of any confidence leading up to even now. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nBy Sunday, large scale ridging builds into our west, heralding in \nnortherly flow and a broad area of surface high pressure. This \ntranslates to quieter and cooler conditions, with highs on Sunday and\nMonday only reaching the low 80s, while overnight lows fall into the\nlow 60s/upper 50s. Unfortunately, this reprieve is short lived as \nthe bulk of the ridge continues to push east into our area, bringing \na return temperatures in the low 90s by mid week. A disturbance to \nour north looks to bring the next chances for precipitation mid-week \nas it drags a cold front through the Great Lakes region, though we're\nstill a bit far out for details.",
